# PR #454 Review

## Findings

1. MUST-FIX — `src/export/triage.ts`: `exportTriageRecords(records, "json")` returns an envelope object (`{ format, items, total }`), but `@triage-agent-export ac-2` and the linked task notes describe JSON export as a JSON array of full `TriageRecord` objects. This is a spec-alignment mismatch, and the AC annotations in the new module currently claim coverage for behavior that is not implemented.

2. MUST-FIX — `tests/triage-export.test.ts`: the AC-2 test asserts the envelope shape, which codifies the mismatch above and prevents the test from catching the spec violation.

3. SHOULD-FIX — `tests/triage-export.test.ts`: the ISO timestamp regex uses an unescaped `.` before milliseconds, so the test can pass invalid timestamps (e.g. `...00X123Z`). It should use `\\.` to enforce the decimal separator.

## Checks Run

- `gh pr diff 454`
- `gh pr view 454 --json title,body,files`
- `kspec task get @implement-triage-agent-export`
- `kspec item get @triage-agent-export`
- `kspec validate` (repo-wide existing alignment/completeness warnings; no `@triage-agent-export` / `@trait-json-output` coverage warning observed)
- `npx vitest run tests/triage-export.test.ts tests/daemon-api-triage.test.ts` (44 tests passed)

